title: KeptUnderWrapsDay3
position: 83,279
---
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
I stare at the "TRANSMITTED" confirmation until the letters blur.
<<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
Each report I falsify adds another layer between me and the person I'm supposed to be. I <color=\#FF8888>feel the gap widening</color>.
But the alternative... typing {$catName}'s name into a document with the word "eradication" in it... isn't something I can do. Not anymore.
<<jump EndDay3>>
===

title: EndDay3
position: 918,14
---
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<hide MonitorSilhouette>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
<<play_music MainTheme>>
The day is winding down. The ship settles into its nighttime hum, a frequency I've memorized without meaning to.
    -> (turn off the monitor)
        <<hide_all_objects>>
        <<show PCRoom>>
        <<if $posSelfPerception > $negSelfPerception>>
            The conversations are changing me. I can feel it. Something that was locked is starting to open, and I'm not sure I can close it again even if I wanted to.
        <<else>>
            I sit in the dark for a while, caught between the person the mission needs me to be and the person these conversations are turning me into.
        <<endif>>
        <<hide_all_objects>>
        <<show PCRoom>>
        <<fade_transition 3>>
        <<wait 3>>
        <<if $day3KeptUnderWraps == true>>
            <<jump DreamDay3>>
        <<else>>
            <<jump StartDay4>>
        <<endif>>
===

title: DreamDay3
position: 915,500
---
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
<<show Stars>>
<<show Sitting>>
The dream starts with a sound I haven't heard in years: my mother's voice, calling me in for dinner.
I'm standing in the backyard of the house I grew up in. The grass is too green, the sky too wide, the way memories overcompensate for detail.
She's at the door. I can see her shape but not her face. The dream won't give me that much.
I remember the last conversation before I left. How I told her this was what I wanted. How she said she understood. How neither of us believed the other.
The training center was easier. There, loneliness had a schedule. Wake, train, eat, sleep. No one asked how you felt because feelings were a variable you learned to control.
I remember the day they told me I was selected. The pride that lasted exactly one hour before it turned into something heavier.
I packed one box. Everything I owned fit inside it.
    -> (hold onto the memory)
        I let myself stay in the backyard a moment longer. The grass under my feet feels real. The air smells like cut lawn and possibility.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        The memory fills me with <color=\#88FF88>a tender ache that feels like proof I'm still alive</color>.
    -> (let it fade)
        I turn away from the door. Some things are easier at a distance. I chose that distance for a reason.
        <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
        The memory dissolves and leaves <color=\#FF8888>a familiar numbness</color> in its place.
The dream shifts. The backyard becomes a viewport. The grass becomes stars.
My mother's voice becomes static.
And somewhere in the static, I think I hear {$catName}.
<<fade_transition 3>>
<<wait 2>>
<<jump StartDay4>>
===
